{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>and that which was prepared</b> — it is past tense from the niphal, and it is missing a vav, and the sense is ונעשה (and it was done), and it means preparation, like: \"and he hastened to do it.\"" "<b>and once in ten days</b> — from this we learn that one day out of ten this feast would be prepared, and he would expend wine in abundance, to be much without deficiency." "<b>yet with all this, the bread of the governor I did not demand</b> — for the meat and wine were plentiful, but the bread was little and not fitting for a governor, because of the famine, and I did not demand of the people, like the former governors, to give me." "<b>upon the people</b> — like אל העם (to the people)."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:08.697380202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}